<item>
            <title>[LU-20848] lnetctl net show returns success for invalid options</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20848</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&quot;lnetctl net show --bogus&quot;&lt;/tt&gt; prints an error but exits with status 0.&lt;br/&gt;
This is incorrectly passing failing tests in our internal tests.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$ lnetctl net show --bogus
net show: show networks
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; --net: net name (e.g. tcp0) to filter on
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; --verbose: display detailed output per network. Optional argument of &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;2&apos;&lt;/span&gt; outputs more stats
$ echo $?
0
&#160;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
